# Scalability Standards

## Data Fetching

- Use Server Components for all data-fetching pages — zero client JS overhead
- Paginate all list queries: never fetch unbounded result sets
- Use Supabase `.range()` for pagination, not client-side slicing
- Add database indexes for any column used in WHERE, ORDER BY, or JOIN
- Use `.select()` to fetch only needed columns, not `select *`

## Real-time

- Use Supabase Realtime only where live updates are essential (Live Event Mode, notifications)
- Unsubscribe from channels on component unmount
- Debounce high-frequency telemetry updates on the client side

## Error Handling

- Every Server Action must return `{ success: true, data } | { success: false, error }`
- Never expose internal error details to the client
- Log errors server-side with enough context to debug (entity ID, user ID, action name)

## Images and Media

- Use Next.js `<Image>` component for all images (automatic optimization)
- Store media in Supabase Storage with signed URLs
- Use appropriate image sizes: thumbnails for lists, full-size only on detail pages
